<article class="env-definition" id="0A5S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A5S">Definition <span data-tag="0A5S">15.71.1</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $K$ be an object of $D(R)$. We say $K$ has <em>finite injective dimension</em> if $K$ can be represented by a finite complex of injective $R$-modules. We say $K$ has <em>injective-amplitude in $[a, b]$</em> if $K$ is isomorphic to a complex </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \ldots \to 0 \to I^ a \to I^{a + 1} \to \ldots \to I^{b - 1} \to I^ b \to 0 \to \ldots  \]
</div>
  <p> with $I^ i$ an injective $R$-module for all $i \in \mathbf{Z}$. </p>
</article>